flow Recover
note """
Step 4.4's fixture: the flow whose datum must survive its owning pod's deletion.

THE TRANSFORM IS THE WHOLE POINT. It carries a checkpoint clause so a record is
journaled for every datum that reaches it, and it is marked idempotent so the
record anchors on ARRIVAL rather than completion. Arrival is what makes recovery
observable end to end: resume hands the record back to this same node on the
SURVIVING pod, which runs it again and carries the datum through to the sink, so
the sink's token proves the datum COMPLETED rather than that a record moved.

A completion anchor would prove much less here. It would re-inject the node's
output into the successors without re-running the node, which is correct for a
non-idempotent node and is not the shape carry-in (e) asks about.
"""
on error Alert
source ingest Feed()
transform hold Hold from ingest
  checkpoint machine.GobCodec[Job]{}
  idempotent
sink finish Done from hold
